# Fountain Court
# A paved court before the front door, holding a dry fountain crusted with last summer's leaves. The greenhouse glimmers palely to the west; a squat brick shed hunches to the east; the front door of the house is north.

> n
[OK]
text
Entrance Hall
The heart of the house: a cold marble floor, a dead fireplace under a wide mantel, and a tall case clock standing silent against the stairs. Doors lead west to the study and east to the kitchen; a colder passage runs north.

You can see a grey overcoat and Mrs Kettle here.

Mrs Kettle blocks your way!

You step out of the wind, and your ears sing in the sudden quiet.

The house holds its old hush — mothballs, cold ash, and wax.
end text
